-- ============================================================================
-- PD4 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Rod Pump Design, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE STRING AND THE GEOMETRY. Four objects make a beam
-- pump, and three of them can be settled completely before a single time step
-- is taken. A spring rate is a sum of compliances. A buoyed weight is
-- Archimedes. A natural frequency is an eigenvalue of a stepped bar. A stroke
-- is a four-bar linkage closed at 720 crank angles. A fluid load is a
-- differential times an area. A displacement is a volume per stroke. NOTHING
-- IN THAT LAYER KNOWS WHAT TIME IT IS, and that is exactly why it is the first
-- tier: a learner who cannot say what a design HAS before it moves cannot read
-- what the march does to it.
--
-- THE TIER IS BUILT ON ONE SENTENCE: EVERY NUMBER HERE IS CLOSED FORM, AND
-- CLOSED FORM IS NOT THE SAME AS CERTAIN. Two of the six have a plausible
-- wrong answer sitting right beside the right one, and neither wrong answer
-- announces itself.
--
--   A STEPPED STRING HAS TWO NOTES AND ONLY ONE OF THEM IS THE STRING'S. The
--   uniform fundamental and the tapered fundamental differ by the taper factor,
--   and both are returned, in the same object, under names one letter apart.
--   A design checked against the wrong one is checked against a string that
--   was never run.
--
--   AND THE TEXTBOOK STROKE IS A SMALL ANGLE APPROXIMATION NOBODY LABELS AS
--   ONE. Twice the crank radius times the front arm over the rear arm is the
--   figure every handbook opens with. On the teaching unit it is 9.93 in short
--   of the four-bar closed properly, which is eight percent of the stroke,
--   because a pitman of finite length is not a rigid link of zero mass. The
--   engine closes the linkage. The handbook does not, and the handbook does
--   not say so.
--
-- WHAT THE TIER MUST NOT OVERSTATE. A rod string is built from a CATALOG, and
-- the catalog's published weights include couplings, so the acoustic velocity
-- a design runs on is the bare steel velocity divided by the square root of a
-- coupling allowance of 1.087. That allowance is a convention about hardware,
-- not a property of steel, and the wave speed a course quotes is only as good
-- as the catalog it came out of. The same discipline applies to the rated
-- displacement: it is a RATING, the largest number this pump can be made to
-- produce, and every factor that makes it smaller belongs to the tier above.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the string, the
-- linkage and the pump as OBJECTS. Not one of this tier's six answers is
-- carried forward as a number, because the tier above restates every condition
-- from the raw geometry and recomputes what it needs.
-- ============================================================================

values ('rodpump', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-a-well-on-a-beam","title":"A Well on a Beam","lesson_keys":["l01-what-a-rod-pump-is","l02-what-this-engine-models","l03-what-it-refuses","l04-four-objects-one-well"]},{"key":"m02-the-rod-string","title":"The Rod String","lesson_keys":["l01-a-taper-is-a-compromise","l02-stiffness-adds-in-series","l03-buoyed-weight","l04-what-a-string-weighs","l05-what-a-string-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m03-the-string-has-a-note","title":"The String Has a Note","lesson_keys":["l01-natural-frequency","l02-a-stepped-bar","l03-why-the-note-matters","l04-what-the-note-does-not-promise"]},{"key":"m04-the-linkage","title":"The Linkage","lesson_keys":["l01-four-bars-and-a-crank","l02-the-stroke","l03-position-and-velocity","l04-what-geometry-decides","l05-what-a-linkage-refuses"]},{"key":"m05-the-pump-itself","title":"The Pump Itself","lesson_keys":["l01-fluid-load","l02-plunger-area","l03-rated-displacement","l04-volume-per-stroke","l05-what-a-rating-is-not"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
